  <Sequence sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText="This workflow looks for a specific string (in_Pattern) in a PDF file (in_FileName). In case the string is found, then  returns a part (out_PDFText) of the total characters which are contained in a pdf file and the out_PatternFound is set to true. In case the specific string is not found, the out_PatternFound is set to false.&#xA;&#xA;Prerequisite is the loading of the UiPath.PDF.Activities package.&#xA;This workflow implements two methods. The fast one (by using the activity Read PDF Text) and the slow one (by using the activity Read PDF with ocr)&#xA;If the fast one is not working then it uses the second one. In case that both methods are not working then an appropriate log message is produced.&#xA;&#xA;Notices:&#xA;   1. In case of &quot;Πρακτικό Παραλαβής&quot;, the Order Number is mentioned twice in the document. Sometimes the first Order Number was correctly detected but not the second. This case was leaded to a faulty Order Number. For this reason the PDFText was limited to the first 350 characters (in that way the second detected Order Number is excluded from the text). In the future is has to be decided whether the number of the characters shall be set to a variable.&#xA;&#xA;   2. In the current implementation the order number has the form &quot;0123-XXXXX&quot;, where the XXXXX is a number. A specific check is performed in order to secure the correct format of the order number (see the .&#xA;&#xA;Troubleshooting:&#xA;   1. The order number is not exctracted &#xA;       i. Try to reconfigure the activity Read PDF with OCR or/and the parameters of Tesseract OCR. It has been tested that the result was better as much as the parameter &quot;scale&quot; was increased. Another critical issue has to do with the &quot;Language&quot; parameter. Because in the current implementation, the order number it's a number, no problem was experienced. But we noticed that the quality of the OCR regognition was very poor concerning a greek text. So, in case in_Pattern is not a number, then the &quot;Language&quot; parameter has to be investigated in depth. &#xA;     Update 4/2/2026. Due to an issue, the  &quot;Language&quot; parameter was set to 'el'. The outcome was better than expected according to the previous paragraph. Also when the &quot;Profile&quot; parameter was set to 'scan', the outcome was more accurate. Those improvments allowed the reduction to '2' of the 'scale' parameter. Keep in mind that as smaller as the 'scale' parameter is set, as shorter is the time needed to get a result from the OCR engine. A special folder has been created in Documentation in order to keep record of the developer debugging.&#xA;&#xA;      ii. Increase the dpi of the scanner (if possible)" sap:VirtualizedContainerService.HintSize="722,2864.8" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_5">
